# Kept out of the Docker build context (COPY . . in apps/api/Dockerfile and
# apps/web/Dockerfile) so the context stays small and nothing stale/local
# leaks into the image. Each Dockerfile re-COPYs its own node_modules from
# its deps/build stage, so excluding node_modules here is safe.

# Dependencies (reinstalled in the deps stage from the lockfile)
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output (rebuilt in the build stage)
.next
**/.next
dist
**/dist
apps/api/src/generated
.turbo
**/.turbo

# Version control / editor / OS
.git
.gitignore
.vscode
.idea
*.DS_Store

# Env files — never bake secrets into an image; they're injected at runtime
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.production.example
!.env.staging.example

# Local dev artifacts
*.log
npm-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
coverage
**/coverage
.dockerignore
**/Dockerfile

# The generated repository index — documentation for humans and agents, never
# read at runtime by the API or the web app. Keeping ~2MB of markdown out of
# the build context speeds every image build and puts nothing in the image
# that could go stale there.
docs/index
